      "text": "Catalog Description"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "An introduction to finance including organization, taxes, capital markets, the commercial banking system, interest rates, financial analysis, financial forecasting, working capital management, marketable securities, accounts receivables, inventories, and short term credit instruments. Students will use financial calculators and/or software applications to apply concepts. Prerequisite: ACC 175."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Learning Outcomes"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "To gain an understanding of the key principles in finance and through practical problem solving learn to appreciate the link between theory and practice."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Teaching/Learning Strategies:"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "A lecture format will be followed with student class participation expected. The student is expected to read assigned chapters and/or lecture notes before class."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Required: "
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "TI-84 or some other financial calculator.  "
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Ability to use, save and upload Microsoft Excel files."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": " "
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Evaluation Methods"
    },
