    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Academic Integrity Statement"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Students are required to abide by the Academic Integrity Policy (https://goo.gl/CBD2qJ) of"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Endicott College."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Body",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "I take proper academic conduct seriously, as it is unfair to other students when cheating goes unpunished. It is important that the work assessed in this course is your own. Any plagiarism or cheating will result in a failing grade in the course, and all violations will be reported to the Dean of the Gerrish School of Business and to the Associate Dean for Academic Success. Please consult with me prior to the start of week two if you are unclear about proper academic behavior and what constitutes misconduct, or if you do not know the difference between plagiarism and paraphrasing. "
    },
    {
      "style": "Body",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading 2",
      "alignment": "LEFT (0)",
      "text": "Paraphrasing vs Plagiarism"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Put very simply, you are required to write in your own words for this course. All assignments should be written individually. This means that you should not be working with any other student, nor should you be copying assignments submitted in past semesters (by you or by any other student). If you are taking ideas from other places (e.g., from a journal article), you need to acknowledge the source (using proper APA style referencing) AND you need to write in your own words to cite that source. Just changing a few words here and there does not constitute proper paraphrasing. "
    },
    {
      "style": "Body",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Body",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Copying from a source and changing a few words so that it is not a direct copy and paste is still plagiarism. Proper paraphrasing involves reading something, thinking about it, interpreting it, synthesizing it with other things you have learned and then writing your own sentences without having to look back at the original source. Please do not be shy to approach your professor and say that you don\u2019t quite know how to do that. Your professor is more than happy to help you if you ask for help!"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "TurnItIn Statement"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "TurnItIn software will be used to check all written assignments submitted in this course. Please read the following statement regarding use of TurnItIn:"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "\nBy taking this course, students agree that all required assignments\u00a0may be\u00a0subject to submission for\u00a0\"similarity review\" to\u00a0Turnitin.com, a tool intended to not just detect instances of plagiarism, but to prevent it as well. The tool is intended to help students identify passages that are unoriginal, incorrectly cited, or lacking appropriate source information. Submitted assignments may also be archived in the\u00a0Turnitin.com\u00a0database for the purpose of checking for possible future instances of plagiarism, additional similarity searches, and other educational purposes at the discretion of the instructor.\u00a0For more information,\u00a0please review the Privacy and Security guide at Turnitin.com. \u00a0"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
